Stimuli for on003825 (Grootswagers et al. 2022 THINGS-EEG)
==========================================================

This folder holds the 26,107 images of the THINGS image database (Hebart et al. 2019), one folder per
concept (1,854 concepts):

    stimuli/
      <concept>/
        <concept>_<NN><b|n|s>.jpg
      stim-things_image.json          # BIDS stimulus sidecar
      README

The events of the 50 participants use 22,448 distinct images; the `stim` column of every events.tsv gives the path
relative to the dataset root and all of them resolve here. They are redistributed here with permission obtained by the NEMAR curator of this dataset (Bruno Aristimunha) for the THINGS image database, whose licence otherwise forbids redistribution without the consent of the copyright owners.

The same archive is distributed by the THINGS project on OSF (https://osf.io/jum2f/, `images_THINGS.zip`, password
at https://osf.io/j6a3m). `python code/smoke_test.py` from the dataset root checks that every events.tsv path
resolves to an image.

License
-------
The THINGS image-database licence (https://osf.io/52wrx/download) limits
use to research / educational purposes and forbids commercial use and
further redistribution or modification without consent of the copyright
owners. The images are not covered by this dataset's licence.

Citations
---------
- Grootswagers, T., Zhou, I., Robinson, A., Hebart, M., & Carlson, T.
  (2022). Human electroencephalography recordings from 50 subjects for
  22,248 images from 1,854 object concepts. Data in Brief.
  https://doi.org/10.18112/openneuro.ds003825.v1.1.0
- Hebart, M.N. et al. (2019). THINGS: A database of 1,854 object concepts
  and more than 26,000 naturalistic object images.
  PLoS ONE 14(10): e0223792. https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0223792
